## Goal
The ELITE (powered-up) versions of the six chapter-5 enemies (shattered porcelain/obsidian dolls of the time prison: violet/indigo bodies, gold kintsugi cracks, mirror shards, magenta eyes). Tripo credits ran out, so the game re-uses each normal enemy's rigged body (with a darker, more cracked texture) and bolts these extra BLENDER PIECES onto its bones, plus a bigger main weapon. Design brief from the level design: "more broken, gold cracks spreading, VIOLET RIFT CRYSTALS bursting out of the body". So every piece is about jagged violet `crystal` clusters and `night_sky` rift slits with `crack_gold` rims and `mirror` shards erupting from the body, held by `gold` kintsugi clamps.

The enemies are chunky 2-head-tall chibi dolls. Design every piece for a **2.2 m tall** reference doll (the game scales by height / 2.2):
- head: centre about Z 1.65, radius ~0.42 (huge head, top ~Z 2.1); the face is on the FRONT (+Y) of the head — never cover the face.
- shoulder joints X ±0.30, Z 1.15; torso ~0.6 wide, ~0.45 deep (Y -0.22 .. +0.22), chest front at Y +0.22
- hips joint Z 0.8.

Coordinates for every ARMOR piece: Blender Z-up, **+Y = the doll's FRONT**, **+X = the doll's RIGHT side**. Each piece's ORIGIN is the ATTACH POINT given below (the game puts the origin on that bone), NOT the bottom centre. Each piece = ONE joined mesh exported to `Game/Assets/Art/Characters/Ch5/Kit_EP_<Name>.fbx`. At least 4 materials, bevels on hard edges, no detail thinner than ~0.03 m, chunky, cel-shade friendly, under ~3000 triangles each. Pieces must read clearly from a high top-down camera (~55 deg), so put most of the volume UP and OUT (above shoulders, behind the back, on top of the head), not in front of the face.

## Armor pieces (shared by all six elites; the game picks a subset per enemy)
1. `ShoulderRift_R` — origin = right shoulder joint. A cluster of 4-6 jagged violet `crystal` spikes (0.15-0.45 long, faceted, pointing up and outward 20-50 deg from vertical) bursting out of a cracked `void_stone_dark` base plate (0.32 x 0.28, sitting ON TOP of the shoulder at Z +0.08), held by a `gold` kintsugi clamp band with `crack_gold` seams; 2 small `mirror` shards stuck between the crystals; one tiny crystal chip hovering 0.12 m above the tallest spike (joined). Extends from X -0.05 to +0.35.
2. `ShoulderRift_L` — exact mirror of `ShoulderRift_R` across X.
3. `BackRift` — origin = upper-chest bone (Z ~1.15, centre of the torso). On the BACK (Y -0.24 .. -0.45): a tall jagged vertical RIFT slab (0.10 thick, 0.55 wide, from Z -0.15 to +0.85 relative to origin, lightning-shaped outline) of `night_sky` with 6-8 `starlight` dots on its back face, outlined by a raised `crack_gold` rim, with 5-7 violet `crystal` spikes and 3 `mirror` shards erupting from its edges, rising above the head height behind the doll so it reads from above; a `gold` clamp bracket (0.3 x 0.06 x 0.25) connecting it to the back at the origin height.
4. `HeadShards` — origin = head bone (the head centre is ~0.30 above the bone, Z +0.30). A broken CROWN of violet `crystal` shards erupting from the TOP-BACK of the head: 5-7 spikes (0.15-0.4 tall) on an arc from ear to ear over the back half of the skull (centred around Y -0.1, Z +0.62..+0.72), a thin `gold` crack-ring segment (radius 0.36, back half only) linking their bases with `crack_gold` seams, one `magenta` gem at the centre back. Keep everything at Y <= +0.10 so the face stays clear.
5. `HipShards` — origin = hips bone. A ring of 6 downward-pointing `mirror`/`crystal` shard tassets hanging from a `gold` cracked belt band (radius 0.32, Z -0.02 .. +0.06) at the sides and back only (no shards on the front centre, X -0.12..+0.12 front is left empty), each 0.18-0.32 long, slight outward flare; `crack_gold` seam on the belt.
