## Goal
HAND-HELD WEAPONS for chapter-5 enemies (shattered porcelain-and-obsidian dolls of the time prison: violet/indigo bodies, gold cracks, mirror shards, magenta eyes) and for the final boss. The characters are rigged separately WITHOUT weapons; the game parents each weapon to the enemy's hand bone, so:
- Each weapon is ONE joined mesh, exported to `Game/Assets/Art/Characters/Ch5/Kit_W_<Name>.fbx`.
- ORIGIN = the exact centre of the GRIP (where a closed fist holds it). The weapon's LONG AXIS points along +Z from the grip (blade / muzzle / head direction = +Z), the "edge" or "front" faces +Y. Anything behind the hand (stock, pommel) goes to -Z.
- Grip is a clear cylinder ~0.045 m radius, ~0.18 m long, centred on the origin along Z, in `wood_dark` or `iron_dark` with a `gold` or `magenta` band so the hand area reads.
- Chunky toy-like proportions (characters are 2-head-tall chibi dolls about 2.2 m tall), cel-shade friendly, no detail thinner than ~0.03 m, bevels on hard edges, at least 4 materials each. Motifs: mirror shards, gold cracks, star/constellation, broken clock parts.

## Pieces (overall length along Z, including the part behind the grip)
1. `ShardRifle` (1.3 m; muzzle at +Z 0.9, stock to -Z 0.4) for the Shard Gunner: a long rifle whose barrel is a bundle of 3 angular `mirror` glass shards bound by `gold` rings, `violet_dark` stock with `crack_gold` crack inlays, a `magenta` crystal ammo cell in front of the grip, a small `gold` star sight on top.
2. `StarStaff` (1.6 m; head at +Z 1.25, butt at -Z 0.35) for the Constellation Witch: an `indigo` staff with `gold` ring bands; the head is a small open armillary: two crossed `gold` rings (diameter 0.45) around a central `starlight` star (5-point, chunky) with 3 small `crystal` orbs linked to it by straight `gold` bars (a mini constellation), `magenta` gem below the head.
3. `RuinMaul` (1.5 m; head at +Z 1.15, pommel -Z 0.35) for the Collapse Giant: a huge two-handed maul whose head is a broken block of `void_stone` (0.7 x 0.45 x 0.45) wrapped in `gold` bands, with `crack_gold` cracks glowing through it and a chunk of `marble` capital stuck on one face, two pebbles hovering off the top; `iron_dark` haft with `gold` rivets.
4. `RiftBlade` (0.85 m; tip at +Z 0.7) for the Rift Assassin (used in both hands): a curved single-edged blade made of a long `mirror` shard (front face `mirror`, back `mirror_back`) with a jagged `crack_gold` crack line along it, a `violet_dark` handle wrap, a small `gold` crescent guard, `magenta` pommel gem.
5. `RiftCenser` (1.5 m; head at +Z 1.15, butt -Z 0.35) for the Rift Caster: a `violet_dark` staff topped by a hanging cage-lantern (`gold` bars, 0.35 tall) holding a jagged floating crack crystal (`night_sky` core with a `crack_gold` outline and `starlight` specks), a short `gold` chain under it, `magenta` tassel bead.
6. `TimeScythe` (2.9 m; blade head at +Z 2.3, butt -Z 0.6) for the final boss "Master of Time" (a cloaked clock-headed reaper): long `indigo` snath with `gold` ring bands and a second grip; at the top a big `dial_face` CLOCK DISC (diameter 0.75, `dial_mark` raised 12 tick bars and two hands, `gold` bezel) from which a huge curved scythe blade (1.4 m, `violet_dark` body, `gold` edge band, a `crack_gold` crack running along it, sharp tip) sweeps to +X; a small hourglass (`gold` frame, `crystal` bulbs) hanging from the disc on a short chain; `gold` spike butt.
7. `MirrorPistol` (0.42 m; muzzle at +Z 0.3, grip pommel -Z 0.1) for the mid-boss "Cat in the Mirror" (a mirror copy of the player's revolver): a chunky toy revolver with a silver-blue `mirror` body with `crack_gold` cracks, `gold` cylinder and trigger guard, `violet_dark` grip, `magenta` gem in the hammer.

Keep each under ~3500 triangles (TimeScythe ~5000). Print `EXPORTED <Name> <tris> <dims>` per piece and `DONE`.
Preview: all weapons standing side by side (grip at the same height), 1800x1000, Workbench flat material colours, camera from the front slightly above, to `Art/tools/specs/blender_kit_ch5_weapons_preview.png`; mark each origin with a small red cross ONLY in the preview (do not export it).
